TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"retry","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate \"conflict-domains\" because attempt 1 left the assigned lane at the prepared base with nothing to own: the worktree is clean, HEAD is still 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, the task diff is empty, and neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh nor any new file under tests/ exists on disk, so the accompanying 10 s finalMessage projection timeout is a downstream symptom of an attempt that ended without committing rather than an independent machinery fault. The whole remedy sits inside the authorized prefixes scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/, so attempt 2 should redo the work and land it. Steering for attempt 2: (1) Write scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh (bash shebang, set -euo pipefail, REPO_ROOT from dirname, IMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\", podman run with --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host and -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\", heredoc'd python payload) after reading specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md, and specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md. (2) BOUNDARY HAZARD — authorized-comment 7 instructs staging results/receipts/proxy.json, but results/ is NOT in this task's conflict domains; staging that path is exactly what the conflict-domains gate rejects on the next attempt. run-proxy.sh must still WRITE results/receipts/proxy.json at runtime (the acceptance argv greps the literal string 'results/receipts/proxy.json' out of the script), but the generated receipt must not be added to the commit. scripts/receipts-verify.py only validates the *.json files that happen to be present, so leaving proxy.json untracked keeps tests/test_repo_invariants.py green. Stage only scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and paths under tests/. (3) Carry the substantive fixes already established by steering: serve text-only with --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' to avoid the vision-encoder profiling allocation, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0 (superseded; integrated_gpu=False on this host), optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True, and record the flag choice in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. Serve with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, request one greedy completion, assert finite logits through the API, and shut down cleanly. (4) Reuse the fork's own tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout to synthesize the /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy checkpoint (same architecture identifier as the workload, a few layers, 8 block-FP8 experts with weight_block_size 128 by 128, small lookup table with the shard tensor name the mmap path expects) instead of writing a fresh generator; the existing /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy tree and the flashnext:dev image survive from prior attempts and should not be rebuilt if valid. (5) Terminal sequence, in order and without exception: run the acceptance argv `bash -euc \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"` and observe it pass; git add only the in-domain paths; git commit; then confirm `git status --porcelain` reports nothing before emitting the final message. An uncommitted worktree at exit reproduces this exact failure."}
